CHECKLIST (Channel-Specific Visual Cues)
Glomeruli
Core Signal: Red (Nestin)+ in a reticular or linear pattern, outlining the capillary tuft (podocyte marker).
Boundary: Enclosed within a distinct Magenta (Perlecan) / Grey (Collagen IV) ring (Bowman's capsule).
Note: Typically lacks internal Green (CD227) signal.

Distal Tubules / Collecting Ducts (DT/CD)
Core Signal: Strong Green (CD227/MUC1)+, often distinctively outlining the apical/luminal surface.
Morphology: Smaller caliber with a regular, circular lumen.
Boundary: Defined by a clear Magenta/Grey basement membrane ring.

Proximal Tubules (PT)
Core Signal: Negative for Green (CD227) (key differentiator from DT/CD).
Morphology: Larger caliber with an irregular or stellate lumen; cytoplasm filled with diffuse Blue (CD183) signal.
Boundary: Outlined by Magenta/Grey basement membranes; closely packed architecture.

Blood Vessels (Arteries/Arterioles)
Core Signal: Strong Cyan (aSMA)+ forming a thick, continuous concentric ring (vascular smooth muscle).
Boundary: Multi-layered, concentric Magenta/Grey (Perlecan/ColIV) structures.
Lumen: Smooth, acellular central opening.

Interstitium
Immune Cells: Scattered or clustered Yellow (CD45)+ punctate signals.
Fibrosis/Matrix: Non-vascular Cyan (aSMA)+ fibrils (myofibroblasts) or diffusely expanded Magenta/Grey matrix areas.
Location: The space between adjacent tubules or between tubules and glomeruli.